---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { agent, brand } from '../config/site';
---
<Page
  title="Editorial Standards"
  h1="Editorial standards"
  description="How the guides on this site are written, fact-checked, dated and corrected, and how advertising rules and insurer approvals shape what we publish."
  path="/editorial-standards/"
  crumb="Editorial standards"
  updated="2026-11-06"
>
  <p class="lede">These guides exist to help you make a good decision, even if that decision is not to buy.</p>
  <h2>Who writes and reviews</h2>
  <p>
    Every guide is written or reviewed by a licensed life insurance agent at {brand.name} (Florida license {agent.flLicense}, NPN {agent.npn}).
    Each page shows the date it was last reviewed.
  </p>
  <h2>How we check facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Government benefits are checked against the official source (Social Security, the VA) and linked.</li>
    <li>Sample prices are real quotes. Each one names the insurer, the plan and the date it was quoted.</li>
    <li>Insurer financial-strength ratings show the rating agency and the date checked.</li>
    <li>We avoid words that mislead: we never call private insurance a "government program," "free," or "guaranteed approval" without explaining the waiting period.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Advertising rules and approvals</h2>
  <p>
    Insurance advertising is regulated by each state. Pages that describe specific insurers' products are reviewed and approved by those insurers
    before publishing, and re-approved after changes.
  </p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you spot an error, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. We fix mistakes promptly and update the review date.
  </p>
</Page>
